  "goodToKnow": "Der Zivilist (die Zivilistin) is a civilian, someone not in the armed forces. It's a weak noun: den Zivilisten. Zivil means civilian or civil: in Zivil (in plain clothes), die Zivilbevölkerung (civilian population), das Zivilrecht (civil law). Until conscription was suspended in 2011, young men could do Zivildienst instead of military service; the Zivis were a familiar sight in hospitals and care homes."
